# THE INSTRUMENT EACH COMPOSITION IS FILED UNDER, ONE ROW PER CITATION, RENDERED AS ONE STRING.
#
# ⭐⭐⭐ IT IS THE LAST DECLARED MAPPING THAT RENDERED NOTHING. `composition_citation` named
#    `documentation` on diagrams/domain_objects.sqlc, emitted not one element, and was invisible
#    to every cardinality law because element KINDS are not one to one: `documentation` was
#    already spent by the pools and the lanes, so its count was exact while this table's share of
#    it was zero. That is the defect diagrams/ungoverned.sqlc exists for, and it is the last row
#    that was still in it.
#
# ⛔⛔ WHAT IT LOSES IS THE STRUCTURE AND NOT THE WORDS, WHICH THE COLUMNS SETTLE:
#   `pm.composition_citation` is `(taxonomy, instrument, clause, version)`, four typed fields, not
#   free prose. A `documentation` element carries all four and carries them as ONE STRING, so a
#   reader can read the citation and a tool cannot resolve it. ⭐ Narrower than *everything* and
#   worth being exact about, because the two states owe different repairs.
#
# ⚠️ THE OPEN QUESTION IS THE SCHEMA'S AND NOT THE DIAGRAM'S. `(composition, seq)` is a bare
#   document ordinal where both sibling children of a composition carry a regime handle, and
#   `merge-group-composition` cites ONE instrument while crossing SEVEN regime boundaries. The
#   emission cannot fix that and must not paper over it.
-- asrt:Composition/asrt:citation, flattened to the one string a documentation element can hold.
SELECT c.composition,
       c.instrument
         || coalesce(' clause ' || c.clause, '')
         || coalesce(' (' || c.version || ')', '')
         || ' under ' || c.taxonomy AS cited
FROM (
    :compose(composition/citations.sqlc)
) c
